CORE
JmlInheritedField
--function JmlInheritedField.bump --jml-source src/main/java/JmlInheritedField.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for unqualified inherited-field access in JML.

`counter` (declared in JmlInheritedFieldBase, accessed from
JmlInheritedField.bump) resolves through resolve_jml_expr's
class-hierarchy walk:
  - Symbol-table lookup of <enclosing_class>.<name> fails.
  - Walk the struct's components; if `<name>` matches no
    direct component, follow the synthetic `@<Parent>`
    super-class component to the parent struct.
  - Build a member-access chain rooted at `*this` whose
    levels match the @-component path; the leaf member's
    type comes from the struct's component declaration.
